#
# EP-6. The leak-prevention scanners, before a commit exists rather than after.
#
# Install it once, from the repository root:
#
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# The hook is **advisory**. It runs on the operator's machine, it can be skipped
# with `--no-verify`, and a machine that never installed it never runs it. That
# is exactly why `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the same check: the hook is a
# fast local answer, CI is the one that has to be true.
#
# The command below is byte-identical to the workflow's, minus `--history`. The
# full-history sweep reads `git log -p --all` and is CI's job; running it before
# every commit would make the hook slow enough to be bypassed, and a hook that is
# bypassed protects nothing. A unit test asserts the two command lines still
# match, so they cannot drift apart quietly.
#
# `cd` first because the uv project is `epppsynth/` and git runs hooks from the
# repository root. The scanners resolve every path from the repository root
# themselves, so the working directory only decides which uv project runs.
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/epppsynth" || exit 1
uv run epppsynth scan
